# Browser QA

Follow the project's `docs/contracts/features/browser-qa.md` when present.

Two-layer model: Mode A (deterministic Playwright specs) + Mode B (agentic
browser MCP). A meaningful Mode B defect should normally become Mode A
coverage.

## Modes

- **Mode A** — deterministic, project-owned Playwright specs. Workflows and
  state transitions, not page-load smoke only.
- **Mode B** — agentic exploration with available browser MCP. Do not merely
  replay Mode A.

A meaningful Mode B defect should normally become a Mode A regression test.

## Isolation

Test-owned records only. Preserve demo/seed data. Do not drain shared
queues. Assert against test-owned identity, not global counts.

## Selectors and artifacts

Prefer role/label selectors; sparse `data-testid`. Retain
trace/screenshot/video on failure. Gitignore generated artifacts and auth
state.

Do not add Playwright to projects that are not browser-capable.
